            <profile id="9fbf-ae72-67f5-401d" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, heavy armour and shield. May have a lance (+4 pts); horse (free) or warhorse (+4 pts). On foot: halberd or double-handed weapon (+4 pts). May wear partial plate (mounted free, dismounted +2 pts) or full plate armour (mounted free, dismounted +4 pts). The warhorse may have cloth barding (+4 pts) or plate barding (+6 pts). If no other Army General is taken, a single Colonello may be made Army General (+25 pts). (Armies of Chivalry p.35)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="8cb6-e50c-9773-3f67" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">4+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
