  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="d70c-90a9-097f-0bc9" name="Italian Condotta (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>ITALIAN CONDOTTA ARMIES 1320-1495 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.35-37). Early Army 1320-1400 and Late Army 1400-1495. Free Companies and Swiss allies documented only; Venetian, Florentine, Milanese, Neapolitan and Papal state restrictions documented in unit text only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Italian Condotta - Early Army (1320-1400)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 25-75%, Infantry 0-50% (Artillery from the Infantry allocation, 0-1 light or multi-barrelled gun per 750 pts), Allies 0-25% (Free Companies, documented only). The state (Naples, Milan, Florence, Papal States, Venice etc.) restrictions on troop entries are documented in the unit text and are not enforced.
[Italian Condotta - Late Army (1400-1495)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 25-75%, Infantry 0-50% (Artillery from the Infantry allocation, 0-1 light or multi-barrelled gun per 750 pts), Allies 0-25% (Free Companies; Swiss for Late Venetian/Florentine armies; documented only). The state restrictions on troop entries are documented in the unit text and are not enforced.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
